"alert.aboutTitle" = "SideSpace 1.0.0";
"alert.aboutBody" = "A menu bar tool that arranges the Google Chrome window.\nCompatible with Apple Silicon and macOS 26.0 or later.\n\nIf Chrome is not in front, the shortcut only brings it forward.\nReserve space on the left of the selected display. With one display, always reserve space there. Other displays use the visible area.\n\nThe default shortcut is ⌥⌘A. You can change it in the menu.\nIt does not read page content and does not use the network.";
"alert.welcomeTitle" = "Welcome to SideSpace";
"alert.welcomeBody" = "Choose Allow, then follow this path and turn on SideSpace:

System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility

Select SideSpace in the list and turn on the switch beside it. If SideSpace is not listed, click + at the lower left, choose SideSpace, then turn on the switch.

System Settings describes this permission broadly. SideSpace uses it only to move and resize the Chrome window. It does not read page content, record keystrokes, take screenshots, or use the network. After the switch is on, the default shortcut ⌥⌘A is ready.";
